WEBVTT

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.240
To wrap things up, we'll hear a word from both competitors.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.290
First, the challenger, Date Eiji.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.180
Above all else, I would like to give Ricardo my thanks.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:27.250
After all, he brought the belt all the way from Mexico just for me.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.530
And now the champion, Ricardo Martinez.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.400
I wouldn't...

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.770
expect too much from him.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.340
Now, if both fighters could shake hands.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.540
S-Shake hands?

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.550
Excuse me...

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.560
Hey...

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:15.230
That was the tense scene at the press conference, where the sparks were already flying between the fighters.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.860
The world title match, now three days away,

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.260
will surely be an even more fearsome confrontation.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.620
I-I can't believe how hard it was to breathe while watching that conference.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.620
If I had been there in person, I would have had a heart attack.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.740
Hello, Makunouchi residence.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:37.810
It's me!

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:38.800
Takamura-san?

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.550
You're coming with me for roadwork tomorrow morning.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:42.690
It's gonna be early, so don't be late!

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.580
He never invites me to go running with him.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.820
Why did we go to a park that's so far away?

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.820
We could just run along the riverbank like we always do.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:00.520
Shut up already!

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.820
Should be any minute now.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.010
Any minute now?

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.510
Date-san!

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.340
What's with you guys?

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.800
Kind of out of the way just for roadwork.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.730
This is the old man's course.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:23.840
Long time no see.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.350
We're tagging along.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.100
Whatever you say.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:33.730
I-I watched the press conference!

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.800
It was so nerve-wracking!

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:39.120
You still know how to put on a show, you old dog.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.610
Hey, I was pretty nervous too.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:46.500
Well, I guess it really took a bit of acting to keep things under control.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.450
He gave you your only black mark!

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.220
I bet you wanted to slug him right there!

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:54.340
Date-san would never do that!

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.380
He's not like you, Takamura-san.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.090
Actually, I really was about to slug him one.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.380
I was making a fist before I realized it!

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:06.860
Seriously?

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:09.190
Well, there's a lot to it.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.390
But...

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:13.510
what I said back there was the truth.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.900
I feel very grateful to Ricardo from the bottom of my heart.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.180
It was really cool!

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:22.900
Thanking him for bringing the belt isn't something most people would do.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.210
That's not it.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.830
What I'm really grateful for...

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:34.410
It's been seven years.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.270
<i>Seven years...</i>

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:39.420
<i>that's how long it's been since Date-san first fought the champion.</i>

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.040
Yes,

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.380
seven years...

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.870
For seven years

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:48.490
he's reigned atop the world's summit.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:53.430
He's stronger than he was back then, and he's still my goal.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.070
When I retired, when I made my comeback,

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:00.440
and even the fact that I'm boxing at all right now...

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.400
All of it is because of him.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.450
All of it?

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.450
Yeah.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:09.550
If I didn't have a goal like Ricardo Martinez,

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:12.510
I wouldn't have been able to climb back up this far.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.830
I'm glad he remained the champion these seven years.  {consider switching this line with the next}

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:20.030
From the bottom of my heart...

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.100
<i>I think I'm starting to understand why Date-san</i>

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:29.660
<i>is so fixated on the WBA belt and Ricardo Martinez.</i>

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:33.560
B-By the way, what do you think your chances are?

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.850
Wouldn't fight him if I didn't think I could take him.

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.540
<i>He came right out and said it!</i>

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.900
<i>That's great!</i>

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.820
Unfortunately, I don't really have a plan for beating him.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.590
Nothing?

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:47.900
Lefts, rights, hooks, uppercuts, defense, instincts...

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:51.370
They've all been refined to exceptionally high levels, and he's incredibly well-rounded.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.490
T-Then how are you going to-

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.670
Dumbass!

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:56.600
When you get to the top of the world,

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:59.370
you can't rely on brainy crap like a battle plan for victory!

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.440
Ricardo is really strong!

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:05.070
So if you wanna beat him, you just gotta be stronger!

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:09.380
That's a simple way of looking at it, but it suits you.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.350
What's that supposed to mean?

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.040
It means you've got the right idea...

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:22.500
The years have made him into a real monster of a champion.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:25.620
But I'm not the same as I used to be either.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:30.850
I hope you're looking forward to seeing who gets the belt strapped on him once the match is over.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:34.320
Date-san...

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:43.920
<i>Date-san must have been watching the champion, and chasing him from behind like this the entire time.</i>

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.960
<i>Like a light shining through a seven-year haze...</i>

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.510
<i>He never lost sight of it, followed it, and now he's finally caught up.</i>

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.340
<i>He's amazing.</i>

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.200
<i>Date-san is really incredible.</i>

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:56.930
<i>I'm...</i>

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.420
<i>I'm going to follow Date-san's figure too!</i>

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.790
<i>And</i>

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:02.940
<i>one day...</i>

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:05.900
Date-san!

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.060
Please win!

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:11.900
Please, please become the world champion!

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:21.920
Don't scream outta the blue like that!

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:22.430
Ow!

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.520
You stupid, idiotic moron!

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:23.890
Ow!

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:46.370
Don't turn the lights on.

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:48.040
I'm fine like this.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:55.330
Tomorrow's the day.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:59.650
When the match is over, bring Yuji into the ring.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:01.980
I bet he'll be really happy.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:06.750
Getting held up by his world champion dad in front of tens of thousands of people.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:15.060
This is something you've wanted more than anything else.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.530
All we can really do is watch over you.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:22.520
But let me ask you for one thing...

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:27.150
Please come back safely.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.400
That's the same thing you said to me seven years ago.

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:39.160
You told me

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:43.410
that it was like I never really came back from Mexico.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:47.260
It was in Mexico that Ricardo Martinez

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:50.720
destroyed my confidence and my dignity.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:55.620
When I came home, I found out you'd collapsed, and our child had miscarried.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:59.840
He's like a devil that took everything away from me.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:04.500
But on the other hand, when I was just a shell of myself,

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:08.600
he's the god who helped me find the soul I needed to start boxing again.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:13.730
I'm going to fight a man who's both a god and a devil to me.

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:18.620
Fear, expectation, hope, and anxiety are all swelling up inside me.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:23.330
I guess I'm just making you more nervous.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:26.620
But...

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:28.630
it's weird.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:31.440
It hasn't been like this since I got my scar... {TLC - "Last time" doesn't make sense here}

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.950
Ever since then, it's always throbbed like hell before every match,

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:39.130
but now, the scar on my nose doesn't ache at all.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.930
It's the best proof that I've finally made it.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:43.820
Just a little further...

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:48.270
A little further and I'll have all of my life back.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:51.770
And the final step...

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:56.530
is to beat Ricardo Martinez!

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.000
I will win!

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.640
So I can be who I really am!

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:16.730
This is one hell of a crowd.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:20.800
This is the match between the historic world champion and the leader of the Japanese boxing scene.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:23.560
No boxing fan would pass this up!

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.430
Where'd Ippo go off to?

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:27.720
Maybe he got lost in the crowd.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:30.290
That'd be just like him.

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:37.880
<i>Seeing all these people and this poster makes it feel real.</i>

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:40.650
<i>Date-san's world title match is today!</i>

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:44.490
<i>Please win, Date-san!</i>

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.330
I'm so tense, my heart is pounding!

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:53.120
Why are you getting tense? {Solo-  Italics on you?}

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:56.130
Still, this is an incredible arena!

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:59.300
The seating capacity is 11,000.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:02.290
That's about three times bigger than Korakuen Hall.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.160
This is amazing.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.880
Date-san is going to fight in a place like this.

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:20.280
Do you take off your shoes?

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.660
Yeah, these are called box seats.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:25.960
You don't see laid-back seating like this very often in the boxing world.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.460
And now, before the main event begins,

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:33.900
please turn your attention to the monitors for some highlights from both of our fighters' careers.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:38.170
The WBA World Featherweight Champion, Ricardo Martinez.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:41.630
He became the champion at 21 and first crossed paths

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:44.700
with tonight's challenger in his second title defense.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:45.830
It's Date!

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:47.260
He's so young, he didn't have a beard yet!

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:49.180
What was this match like?

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:52.340
<i>Date-san's first title match...</i>

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:03.680
The first match ended 1 minute and 12 seconds into the second round.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:09.700
Before the champion's overwhelming strength, the challenger's dreams were shattered in the Mexican ring.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.080
What's with this?

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:06.120
It's so one-sided!

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:07.730
And the match is about to start too.

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:09.700
How the hell do you beat a guy like that?

00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:11.570
He's a damn monster.

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:14.830
Instead of getting them warmed up, it's silenced the whole crowd.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:18.660
B-But I'm sure the crowd will get heated up once Date-san's footage runs!

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:20.850
And now the challenger, Date Eiji.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:21.340
See? {jama: added}

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:24.510
After having retired from boxing...

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.510
Date's punches are impressive too!

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.010
That match was hot!

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:28.010
Seeing this raises my expectations!

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.310
S-See...

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:31.950
everyone's better now.

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:33.660
It must be hard for you.

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:38.180
Well, Ricardo does have quite the record after reigning at the top of the world for so long.

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:39.840
No matter how you look at it, the old man's at a disadvantage.

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:40.770
B-But-

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:42.590
That's right!

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:46.570
The old man was knocked off of the world summit once before, but made his way back up a second time.

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:51.010
The guy who stayed at the top against the guy who climbed back up...

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:54.270
Let's see which one's stronger.

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:10.580
Hey... Ippo?

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:13.700
What's with him?

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:15.030
Is he going to the bathroom?

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:20.060
<i>Date-san... {jama: added}</i>

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:22.150
It's Makunouchi!

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.880
The Japanese Champ!

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:25.650
Are you here to give Date your regards?

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.050
Yes.

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:28.790
Excuse me! Coming through!

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:34.430
<i>This must be Date-san's...</i>

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:38.090
G-Good afternoon!

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:40.800
Thanks for coming out, Makunouchi-san.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:41.580
Today...

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:45.900
Today my papa is gonna become the world champion!

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.850
You're Yuji-kun, right?

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:54.240
Everything will be okay!

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.490
Your father's really strong!

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:59.980
I'm sure he's going to become the world champion!

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:01.390
Yes! {jama: added}

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.380
D-Date-san!

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:34.000
Today's match, um...

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:35.940
Makunouchi...

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:39.080
I'll be waiting for you

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:42.070
at the top of the world.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:50.780
<i>I will...</i>

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.510
<i>never forget this!</i>

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:56.620
<i>Never, no matter how far away he gets...</i>

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.770
<i>I'll chase him and chase him, then one day I'll...</i>

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.390
<i>So,</i>

00:15:01.390 --> 00:15:02.910
<i>please win!</i>

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:05.540
<i>Please stay as my goal!</i>

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:07.110
<i>Date-san!</i>

00:15:17.510 --> 00:15:18.670
That took you a while.

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:20.790
You get something to eat?

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:27.070
So, how is the old man?

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:30.270
He's ready to go!

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:31.690
He looks like he's in good condition!

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:33.170
I see...

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:34.830
Alright!

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:35.950
Might as well cheer for him!

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:37.850
Oh, yeah! It's gonna get hot in here!

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:39.200
C'mon, Date-san!

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:44.710
Ladies and gentlemen, we apologize for the wait.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.990
Both competitors will now make their way to the ring!

00:15:56.500 --> 00:16:01.720
From the blue corner, the first to enter is the challenger, Date Eiji!

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:12.220
After seven long years, it's his second world title match!

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:16.740
Following a temporary retirement, he made his way back up from the bottom!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:21.130
He walks the path of glory once more!

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:22.750
And now, with the hearts of the nation behind him,

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:27.790
Japan's Date Eiji stands in the ring!

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:35.760
And now, in the red corner,

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:39.170
the WBA World Featherweight Champion!

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:45.860
Ricardo Martinez!

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:49.300
The myth in action!

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:50.610
The living legend!

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:53.270
Seven years and ten months since he took the throne!

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:55.280
It's his 17th title defense!

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:59.950
A name that will undoubtedly be passed down through boxing history for generations!

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:03.820
The super champion from Mexico!

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:10.670
Ricardo Martinez makes his first appearance in a Japanese ring!

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.150
It's getting tense!

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:18.670
I might not be as bad as Ippo, but my heart's still throbbing!

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:20.690
I-I can't take it!

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:23.140
My heart's going to explode!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.600
<i>I wonder how Date-san feels standing in the ring right now!?</i>

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:36.040
<i>I can't believe how calm he looks.</i>

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:40.110
<i>I'm sure the memories of the last seven years are swirling around in his brain.</i>

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:41.710
<i>Eiji...</i>

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:43.800
<i>you're one hell of a man.</i>

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.620
<i>I'm proud of you.</i>

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.900
<i>Seven years...</i>

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.580
<i>The wait felt both long and short,</i>

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:52.130
<i>but I made it.</i>

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:56.030
<i>All of my answers are here in this ring today.</i>

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:59.340
<i>I was able to make it this far believing in that.</i>

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:02.340
<i>All that's left is to go get them.</i>

00:18:02.340 --> 00:18:03.440
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:05.220
the wait is over.

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:12.260
We will now begin the WBA World Featherweight Title Match.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:14.950
In the red corner,

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:17.590
weighing 125.5 pounds,

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:19.700
from Mexico,

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:23.660
the WBA World Featherweight Champion...

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:28.480
Ricardo Martinez!

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:35.100
In the blue corner,

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:38.130
weighing 125.6 pounds,

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.300
from Nakadai Gym,

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:43.800
the 1st ranked WBA Featherweight...

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:46.310
Date

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:49.290
Eiji!

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:56.590
And now, both fighters head to their corners.

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:59.070
Will the champion's reign continue?

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:01.660
Or will the challenger write himself into the pages of history?

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:04.050
The bell is about to ring!

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:05.930
I don't intend on giving you a game plan.

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.910
Just use your experience and technique to beat the challenger.

00:19:09.510 --> 00:19:14.410
Hopefully, this crowd will see the brilliance of real boxing tonight.

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:17.950
For now, just watch how he starts out.

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:21.170
Don't rush in until you get a grasp of his timing and rhythm.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:24.380
I know,

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:26.930
but I've got to go greet him at least.

00:19:27.590 --> 00:19:29.430
It's been seven years,

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:32.420
so it needs to be one hell of a greeting.

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:34.920
<i>It's starting.</i>

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.410
Now it's begun!

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:43.600
The WBA World Featherweight Title Match!

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:47.700
The two veterans touch gloves in center ring and then get some space!

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:52.790
Who will have his name engraved in history as the strongest featherweight?

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:55.290
They both wait to see how the other will start!

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:08.100
The challenger makes his move!

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:14.060
A left!

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:32.400
Another left!

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:34.790
It lands as the champion's hand was knocked aside!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:38.470
The opening hit is a left from the challenger!
